Troubleshooting Tips
Issue: Permission denied when accessing logs

Solution: Use sudo before grep commands
Auth logs require root privileges
Issue: No output from grep commands

Solution: Check if log file exists: sudo ls -lh /var/log/auth.log
Some systems use /var/log/secure instead
Issue: Script shows "command not found"

Solution: Ensure script is executable: chmod +x scriptname.sh
Run with ./ prefix: ./scriptname.sh
Issue: AWK field numbers seem wrong

Solution: Log format varies by system
Use awk '{print NF}' to count fields
Adjust field numbers accordingly
Issue: Empty results

Solution: Generate activity first (try SSH login, sudo command)
Check if logs are being written: sudo tail -f /var/log/auth.log
